WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.060
What does the test arrangement assume?

00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:08.872
In Setup, open Ground, then Reference option.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:13.451
Select Ideal fixed groundline for a restrained cantilever.

00:00:14.388 --> 00:00:16.263
The model loads the physical tip.

00:00:17.201 --> 00:00:21.209
Match that fixture; a three-point bending test needs a different model.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.145
Under Pole, open Properties.

00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:28.153
Choose a source appropriate to the timber.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:33.574
Here, eight gigapascals and forty megapascals are example assumptions,

00:00:33.832 --> 00:00:34.973
not measured data.

00:00:36.711 --> 00:00:40.773
Enter length, embedment and the three diameters or circumferences.

00:00:41.711 --> 00:00:43.735
Keep the property source with the case.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.836
In Defects, choose a type and press Add.

00:00:49.778 --> 00:00:52.617
Set its height, length, width and depth.

00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:56.924
Position and shape controls place this cavity off centre.

00:00:58.662 --> 00:01:00.211
It removes wood completely.

00:01:01.148 --> 00:01:05.442
Decay instead leaves weakened material, with an illustrative severity-to-strength

00:01:05.455 --> 00:01:06.284
relationship.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:10.746
Choose Stresses and Capacity in kilonewtons.

00:01:11.688 --> 00:01:15.343
Keep Specified load direction, then press Critical section.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.526
Timber bending limit is the whole-pole estimate.

00:01:20.463 --> 00:01:24.499
The height curve shows section capacities; its lowest value locates

00:01:24.512 --> 00:01:27.393
the first bending limit, possibly above ground.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.658
The compass controls the load direction.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.326
Load applied in worst direction searches for a weaker orientation.

00:01:39.264 --> 00:01:41.682
Off-centre damage makes direction important.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.750
The comparison also depends on entered dimensions and material strength;

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:50.229
credible input ranges are part of interpreting this estimate.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.267
Open Menu and Compare A and B to set up matching cases.

00:01:57.209 --> 00:02:02.128
Hold geometry, material and direction constant when comparing deterioration.

00:02:03.065 --> 00:02:06.109
Save case preserves the inputs and property source.

00:02:07.846 --> 00:02:12.466
This beam first-limit estimate is not a validated fracture load; comparison

00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:14.613
with measured tests remains necessary.
